# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: 📱
name: Android Mirror
group: extras
what: Mirror and control your Android phone in a desktop window (scrcpy over wireless adb). Finds the phone's changing port automatically.
why: Use your phone without taking the headset off. Google ships `adb` only for x86, so this installs an aarch64 build that runs on the Frame.
changes: `adb` (Arch Linux ARM, signature-checked) in `~/.local/lib/android-tools`, Homebrew `scrcpy`, `phone` launcher; in VR, two dashboard patches and a control-only scrcpy server on the phone
access: Network connection to your phone's wireless debugging; pairing keys in `~/.android` (plain files: anyone with your user can use them to reach the phone while it has wireless debugging on). adb's server listens on a socket only you can use (not TCP port 5037)
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall adb-scrcpy`
